## DIFC Rules of the Court — Part 38 (Costs)
##
## Source: Rules of the DIFC Courts ("RDC"), Part 38. The Court conducting
## a detailed assessment on the standard basis allows costs that are
## proportionate to the matter, and resolves doubt in favour of the
## paying party. The costs allowed are the sum of the assessed
## professional time (hours × hourly rate) and reasonable disbursements
## (court fees, travel, expert reports, etc.).
##
## Used in:
##   trace-01 — CFI 058/2024 Atul Dhawan v Ramzi Wahib El Jaouhari
##              (RDC 38.7 standard-basis assessment).
##
## This module is the deterministic computational core. Discretionary
## limbs (proportionality, doubt resolution) are *not* encoded here —
## they are the human-judgment limb. The module returns the arithmetic
## once the human inputs (hours allowed, hourly rate, reasonable
## disbursements) are fixed.

```catala
declaration structure CostsClaim:
  data hours_worked content decimal
  data hourly_rate_aed content decimal
  data reasonable_disbursements_aed content decimal

declaration structure StandardBasisAward:
  data professional_time_aed content decimal
  data disbursements_aed content decimal
  data total_aed content decimal

declaration scope StandardBasisAssessment:
  input claim content CostsClaim
  output award content StandardBasisAward

scope StandardBasisAssessment:
  definition award equals
    let pt equals claim.hours_worked * claim.hourly_rate_aed in
    let db equals claim.reasonable_disbursements_aed in
    StandardBasisAward {
      -- professional_time_aed: pt
      -- disbursements_aed: db
      -- total_aed: pt + db
    }
```

## Test — replays the headline computation from trace-01.

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestRDC38StandardBasis:
  composite scope StandardBasisAssessment
  output award content StandardBasisAward

scope TestRDC38StandardBasis:
  definition award equals composite.award
  definition composite.claim equals
    CostsClaim {
      -- hours_worked: 24.00
      -- hourly_rate_aed: 250.00
      -- reasonable_disbursements_aed: 1121.75
    }
  ## RDC 38.7 standard-basis arithmetic from trace-01.
  assertion award.professional_time_aed = 6000.00
  assertion award.disbursements_aed = 1121.75
  assertion award.total_aed = 7121.75
```
